<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">assessment</ansi>

Your company sizes up an enemy group: how the company, as it stands right
now, measures up against the foes you can see. It works before a fight or
during one, is free and instant, and changes nothing.

<ansi fg="yellow">Usage:</ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">scout [group]</ansi>
  The group's formation, then the assessment below it.

  <ansi fg="command">consider [enemy]</ansi>
  The assessment alone, for that enemy's whole group (a lone creature is
  a group of one): <ansi fg="command">consider ruffians</ansi>, or <ansi fg="command">consider ruffian</ansi>.

  Assessment: A hard fight for your company; it could go either way.
    Counted: you, Tamsin Reed and Brother Oswin. Not with you: Ysolde (fled).
    Hurt: Tamsin Reed (badly wounded).
    Can't reach any of them from where they stand: Brother Oswin.
    Out of your company's reach: the bandit slinger.
    Not judged: spells, healing and abilities, hidden foes, and anyone yet to come.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">The words</ansi>

  an easy fight   they should fall quickly
  a fair fight    you should win, likely with some hurt
  a hard fight    close: either side could win
  a grave risk    they are likely to beat you
  hopeless        don't

"It could go either way" means the estimate sits close to even, or close to
the line between two words. "The odds look clear" means it doesn't. There
are never numbers or percentages: it is a judgment, not a promise.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">What it weighs</ansi>

- Who is counted: you and the companions with you now who can fight.
  Fled, fallen, awaiting, and separated companions, and anyone down or
  out of the fight, are listed as not with you. Pets and allies aren't
  counted (it says when an ally is here). With nobody able to fight, it
  is hopeless.
- Health as it is now: wounds (<ansi fg="command">help wounds</ansi>) and hurts lower it.
- Each fighter's gear, stats, defense, and dodge, and burden, which cuts
  dodge (<ansi fg="command">help burden</ansi>).
- Reach, from where each fighter stands in the formation (<ansi fg="command">help formation</ansi>):
  a member who can reach none of them adds nothing, and a foe out of
  everyone's reach can't be hurt yet. Move members with <ansi fg="command">formation</ansi> and
  look again.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">What it can't judge</ansi>

Spells, healing, and class abilities on either side, foes you can't see,
groups waiting their turn, and anyone yet to arrive. In the dark you can't
make them out at all, so there is no assessment.

In the web client, the Combat tab's Battle view shows the same headline as
"Outlook" while you fight (<ansi fg="command">help webclient</ansi>).

See also: <ansi fg="command">help scout</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help consider</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help combat</ansi>.
